  "generated_model": "##### Decision Variables\n\n$x_i \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\geq 0}$: Number of vehicles of type $i$ to order per day, for each $i \\in I$ (where $I$ is the set of all vehicle types listed below).\n\n##### Parameters\n\nLet $I$ be the set of vehicle types:\n- Sedan\n- SUV\n- Truck\n- Convertible\n- Minivan\n- Coupe\n- Hatchback\n- Station Wagon\n- Electric Car\n- Hybrid Car\n- Luxury Sedan\n- Sports Car\n- Crossover\n- Diesel Truck\n- Compact SUV\n- Luxury SUV\n- Cargo Van\n- Pickup Truck\n- Roadster\n- Muscle Car\n- Off-road Vehicle\n- Camper Van\n- Compact Car\n- Motorcycle\n- Electric SUV\n\nFor each $i \\in I$:\n- $v_i$: Profit per unit of vehicle type $i$\n- $w_i$: Inventory weight per unit of vehicle type $i$\n\nParameter values (from products.csv):\n\n| Vehicle Type        | $v_i$ (Profit) | $w_i$ (Weight) |\n|---------------------|:--------------:|:--------------:|\n| Sedan               | 2524           | 99             |\n| SUV                 | 4614           | 55             |\n| Truck               | 8416           | 75             |\n| Convertible         | 5917           | 94             |\n| Minivan             | 9048           | 80             |\n| Coupe               | 1140           | 82             |\n| Hatchback           | 8962           | 71             |\n| Station Wagon       | 1888           | 100            |\n| Electric Car        | 8487           | 28             |\n| Hybrid Car          | 4425           | 93             |\n| Luxury Sedan        | 4717           | 84             |\n| Sports Car          | 4210           | 83             |\n| Crossover           | 1226           | 62             |\n| Diesel Truck        | 7400           | 90             |\n| Compact SUV         | 4639           | 99             |\n| Luxury SUV          | 7712           | 96             |\n| Cargo Van           | 3299           | 21             |\n| Pickup Truck        | 9895           | 39             |\n| Roadster            | 4496         